<title>ZIMBABWE: BA PLANE WHEELS CATCH FIRE AT HARARE AIRPORT.</title>
<headline>BA PLANE WHEELS CATCH FIRE AT HARARE AIRPORT.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The wheels of a British Airways Plc aircraft caught fire after it landed at Zimbabwe's Harare International Airport on Tuesday, state radio reported.</p>
<p>Firefighters battled for 30 minutes to put out the fire on the Boeing 747. Passengers later said the captain told them there was a slight problem with the brakes and one passenger added that the plane's takeoff from London had been delayed while air technicians attended to it, radio said.</p>
<p>British Airways in Harare was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Harare Newsroom +263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
